Financial Performance – Harpal
Harpal has delivered one of the team's most impactful engineering initiatives this year by leading the optimisation of our Middleware container images and driving the migration to UBI 9 Minimal. His work has helped application teams build and release their applications more efficiently while maintaining a stronger security posture.
The results have been significant. Through image optimisation and the adoption of multi-stage builds, Harpal has reduced image sizes by up to 60%. He has also achieved substantial reductions in security vulnerabilities across our Middleware runtime images, eliminating significant number of Critical CVEs in Python and Golang images and reducing High-severity CVEs by 70–75% in Python, Golang and WebSphere Liberty images, and 82% in Tomcat. These improvements have helped reduce the overall attack surface while making our images smaller and more efficient to build, distribute and maintain.
Harpal has also driven the adoption of engineering best practices across the Middleware teams, including multi-stage container builds, removing unnecessary packages and agents from runtime images, and adopting UBI 9 Minimal as the standard base image. In addition, he enhanced the Managed Repos automation to track UBI 8 image release cadences and highlight ageing tags, giving us better visibility of images that need attention.
He has continued to support the UBI delivery pipeline, helping ensure updated base images are released reliably and on time for our development teams. This is important in maintaining a consistent supply of approved and up-to-date base images across our developer community.
As Harpal builds on this success, I would like him to continue driving automation and standardisation across our Middleware images while working closely with product teams to accelerate the adoption of optimised base images. I would also encourage him to build on the Managed Repos automation and look for further opportunities to improve visibility of image familes, image age/size, release cycles and adoption across our portfolio.

